[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: A widget that counts or lists reads the narrative its Over relation names, else itself

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-WIDGET-SUBJECT-IS-ITS-OVER-TARGET
TITLE: A widget that counts or lists reads the narrative its Over relation names, else itself
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: A widget needs to draw over something that is not a narrative, or Over is found used as a dependency.
STATEMENT: >>>
The widgets that draw a figure over other narratives -- strip, tally, index,
list, and grid, stack, ladder, rows when they mirror -- take a SUBJECT: the
narrative named by the widget narrative's Over relation, else the widget
narrative itself. So the Start screen shows a heat strip over the Topics tab,
the type grid over the grid card under Types, and the five gaps over the
Gaps tab, without containing any of them twice.

Over is a Parent role written on the widget narrative. Its target is a
narrative in the same plan or in the spec (INV-NO-EXTERNAL-PLAN-REFS holds
unchanged). It carries no fingerprint and, like PLACE, is outside the
contract hash: it says where to look, not what is true.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Drawing a figure over data that lives elsewhere is what v1's Start did four times; a relation that strictdoc refuses to dangle is the cheapest honest way to say it.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Ruled 2026-08-30 as a first-pass decision under the operator's delegation ('I don't want to be bothered by the recommendation before implementation'); overrule by superseding. Chosen from three independent designs judged against an 82-element inventory of the v1 page. AUTHORED_BY reads llm because the writer has no flag for the human rungs.
<<<
